  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ISA.64.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.64.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh that thou wouldst rend the heavens, that thou wouldst come down, that the mountains might flow down at thy presence,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.64.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.64.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As when",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the melting fire burneth, the fire causeth the waters to boil, to make thy name known to thy adversaries, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the nations may tremble at thy presence!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.64.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.64.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When thou didst terrible things ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " we looked not for, thou camest down, the mountains flowed down at thy presence.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.64.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.64.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For since the beginning of the world ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " have not heard, nor perceived by the ear, neither hath the eye seen, O God, besides thee, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "what",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he hath prepared for him that waiteth for him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.64.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.64.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou meetest him that rejoiceth, and worketh righteousness, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "those that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " remember thee in thy ways: behold, thou art wroth; for we have sinned: in those is continuance, and we shall be saved.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.64.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.64.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But we are all as an unclean ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thing",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and all our righteousnesses ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as filthy rags; and we all do fade as a leaf; and our iniquities, like the wind, have taken us away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.64.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.64.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none that calleth upon thy name, that stirreth up himself to take hold of thee: for thou hast hid thy face from us, and hast consumed us, because of our iniquities.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.64.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.64.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But now, O LORD, thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " our father; we ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the clay, and thou our potter; and we all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the work of thy hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.64.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.64.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be not very wroth, O LORD, neither remember iniquity for ever: behold, see, we beseech thee, we ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all thy people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.64.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.64.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy holy cities are a wilderness, Zion is a wilderness, Jerusalem a desolation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.64.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.64.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Our holy and our beautiful house, where our fathers praised thee, is burned with fire: and all our pleasant things are laid waste.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.64.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.64.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wilt thou refrain thyself for these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", O LORD? wilt thou hold thy peace, and grievously afflict us?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
